WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.038 --> 00:00:04.797
Claudia hurried into the local TV station.

2
00:00:04.798 --> 00:00:12.625
As her prize for winning a local journalism contest, she was going to follow a TV news reporter for the entire day.

3
00:00:12.626 --> 00:00:18.549
"This is going to be awesome!" she thought.

4
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.961
The first part of the day was a morning meeting.

5
00:00:21.962 --> 00:00:27.116
Claudia listened as the news director assigned news stories to reporters.

6
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:31.537
Afterward, a reporter named Meredith Burke approached Claudia.

7
00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:34.893
"You'll be working with me today."

8
00:00:34.894 --> 00:00:38.824
Claudia forced a smile as she shook Meredith's hand.

9
00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:45.648
The reporter seemed very smart, but Claudia had been hoping to work with a reporter covering something exciting.

10
00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:51.220
Meredith had been assigned to a story with a boring topic—road repairs.

11
00:00:51.221 --> 00:00:56.739
Meredith led Claudia over to her desk and reached for a phone.

12
00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:02.855
"First we have to schedule interviews with people who might be affected by the construction.

13
00:01:02.856 --> 00:01:09.411
You might be surprised to learn that a TV reporter spends a lot of time on the phone.

14
00:01:09.412 --> 00:01:12.662
Do you have any questions about the story?"

15
00:01:12.663 --> 00:01:14.895
Claudia shook her head.

16
00:01:14.896 --> 00:01:19.991
She didn't feel interested enough in road construction to have any questions.

17
00:01:19.992 --> 00:01:26.012
Still, she tried to act polite and listen alertly as the reporter made the calls.

18
00:01:26.013 --> 00:01:28.448
Finally Meredith hung up.

19
00:01:28.449 --> 00:01:33.471
"I've arranged to meet with some people in the area near the project.

20
00:01:33.472 --> 00:01:38.445
Let's find Jeremy, my videographer, and get in the van."

21
00:01:38.446 --> 00:01:43.016
"Sounds good," Claudia mumbled.

22
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:50.711
At the roadwork site, Claudia saw construction workers and large vehicles everywhere.

23
00:01:50.712 --> 00:01:55.623
"What do you think we should record, Claudia?" Meredith asked.

24
00:01:55.624 --> 00:02:00.955
"Aren't you going to interview people?" Claudia asked.

25
00:02:00.956 --> 00:02:05.004
"Yes, but we need to record more than just the interviews."

26
00:02:05.005 --> 00:02:13.587
Jeremy nodded. "It would be pretty boring to show people talking about roadwork without showing the actual construction."

27
00:02:13.588 --> 00:02:19.466
Claudia looked around as Jeremy began setting up his camera.

28
00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:25.216
"Well, maybe you could film around the whole construction site?

29
00:02:25.217 --> 00:02:28.601
And also get some close-ups of the road?"

30
00:02:28.602 --> 00:02:37.157
Meredith smiled. "Smart ideas." She began giving more specific directions to Jeremy.

31
00:02:37.158 --> 00:02:44.413
News stories on TV were usually only a couple of minutes long—but Jeremy recorded for much longer than that.

32
00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:49.860
"We'll edit everything back at the TV station," Meredith explained.

33
00:02:49.861 --> 00:02:56.380
"Now it's time to interview some people. What questions should I ask?"

34
00:02:56.381 --> 00:03:02.375
"Um . . . " Claudia thought. "Are you happy with the roadwork?"

35
00:03:02.376 --> 00:03:05.641
"That's an okay way to start.

36
00:03:05.642 --> 00:03:12.494
But yes or no questions aren't very exciting for interviews. What about—"

37
00:03:12.495 --> 00:03:17.881
"How do you feel about the roadwork?" Claudia burst out.

38
00:03:17.882 --> 00:03:25.487
Meredith grinned and showed Claudia her notepad. "That's actually my first question!"

39
00:03:25.488 --> 00:03:33.098
Throughout the morning Claudia observed as Meredith interviewed local residents and business owners.

40
00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:36.777
Everyone had an opinion on the construction.

41
00:03:36.778 --> 00:03:42.748
"I'm glad the city is finally repairing the roads," one woman said.

42
00:03:42.749 --> 00:03:46.046
"It will improve my commute."

43
00:03:46.047 --> 00:03:50.382
"We can't ride our bikes anymore," a kid complained.

44
00:03:50.383 --> 00:03:54.291
"And our bus stop got moved to a different street!"

45
00:03:54.292 --> 00:04:00.828
"The construction is terrible for business," a restaurant owner said.

46
00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:06.308
"I think this is enough," Meredith said after her sixth interview.

47
00:04:06.309 --> 00:04:10.882
"Now we need to record an introduction to the story.

48
00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:18.297
After seeing the site and doing some interviews, I think I know how to report the story to viewers."

49
00:04:18.298 --> 00:04:21.565
Meredith and Jeremy planned out a few shots.

50
00:04:21.566 --> 00:04:25.052
Then she stood in front of the camera with a microphone.

51
00:04:25.053 --> 00:04:31.577
"Local residents have mixed reactions to roadwork on Renard Road . . . "

52
00:04:31.578 --> 00:04:37.733
Back at the station, Meredith led Claudia to an editing room with computer monitors.

53
00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:41.993
"We recorded about two hours of material.

54
00:04:41.994 --> 00:04:47.356
Now we're going to edit it down to a two-minute segment."

55
00:04:47.357 --> 00:04:50.935
Meredith showed Claudia how the software worked.

56
00:04:50.936 --> 00:04:57.811
After she'd finished the video segment, she recorded a few more lines of sound in a recording booth.

57
00:04:57.812 --> 00:05:00.186
"Finished!"

58
00:05:00.187 --> 00:05:05.749
"That was a ton of work for a two-minute story," Claudia said.

59
00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:08.731
"But it was really fun."

60
00:05:08.732 --> 00:05:12.351
"Phew!" Meredith looked relieved.

61
00:05:12.352 --> 00:05:17.802
"I was afraid you might find a story about roadwork boring."

62
00:05:17.803 --> 00:05:25.687
"Maybe at first," Claudia admitted. "But it certainly matters to the people in that neighborhood."

63
00:05:25.688 --> 00:05:31.505
"Ready to see if the news desk has another story for us?" Meredith asked.

64
00:05:31.506 --> 00:05:36.191
"Reporters usually handle several stories in a day."

65
00:05:36.192 --> 00:05:41.316
Claudia was already on her feet.

